                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5966bb90-e1bd-3884-8d94-457c31b348ef",
                        "entry_id": "fbe9de92-f6ac-354a-9da4-c5cd98e4a69a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "анат. внутреннее носовое отверстие у позвоночных животных и человека; в частности, одно из двух отверстий, которые отделены друг от друга задним краем и крыльями сошника, через которые полость носа сообщается с полостью глотки"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "660d8371-0dd9-48cd-828a-f084ddf6f5a2",
                                "sense_id": "5966bb90-e1bd-3884-8d94-457c31b348ef",
                                "text": "Сзади полость носа через хоаны сообщается с полостью носоглотки."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "00a4d700-ac92-4ba5-9e30-0549cb693f35",
                        "source_entry_id": "fbe9de92-f6ac-354a-9da4-c5cd98e4a69a",
                        "source_sense_id": "5966bb90-e1bd-3884-8d94-457c31b348ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "choana",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "choana",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8af25b09-362a-3737-aa49-077a2a538168",
                                        "entry_id": "41a45a0b-8a36-397d-9a83-bb9dfb7ab6a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A funnel; a funnel-shaped opening."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a480df0-5d5d-4bf2-8bf5-060327f22917",
                                                "sense_id": "8af25b09-362a-3737-aa49-077a2a538168",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: infundibulum, pelvis, cornu"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf1bd8e7-740c-305b-85e5-0be1c4385935",
                                        "entry_id": "41a45a0b-8a36-397d-9a83-bb9dfb7ab6a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pair of apertures towards the back of the nasal cavity, opening into the nasopharynx."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1e69526-faba-427c-9a62-ca5de8480e27",
                                                "sense_id": "cf1bd8e7-740c-305b-85e5-0be1c4385935",
                                                "text": "The choanal glands of caecilians open at the margin of the choanae, whereas those of salamanders open deep within the choanae at the margin of the olfactory epithelium."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06127ebd-26b6-4a31-899b-9b613c6a96f6",
                                                "sense_id": "cf1bd8e7-740c-305b-85e5-0be1c4385935",
                                                "text": "Zuckerkandl (1893) gives far and away the greatest measurements for the choanae; Hopmann (1895) reported that in man the choana has a mean height of 27 mm, and a mean width of 13 mm (Merkel, 1896); in women it measures 25 x 12mm. These values agree closely with our findings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e8491b4-adc4-4c50-bfc2-5416bfe1eab4",
                                                "sense_id": "cf1bd8e7-740c-305b-85e5-0be1c4385935",
                                                "text": "Inside of this area it is possible to identify clearly two parallel echonegative zones, which belong to the nasal cavities (choanas) and are placed on both sides of a medial structure, considerably echogenic, which corresponds to nasal bridge (Fig. 2.12.)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e64e1e83-4a1d-47b5-a24d-fe5abce4b583",
                                                "sense_id": "cf1bd8e7-740c-305b-85e5-0be1c4385935",
                                                "text": "The bony rim of the posterior choana is located by passing the 4-mm microdebrider blade through the posterior ethmoids and into the nasopharynx. The tip of the microdebrider blade is pushed against the mucosa just above the bony choanae on the anterior face of the sphenoid."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b943f58f-a6a8-4dcb-9acc-f510cfe32fad",
                        "source_entry_id": "fbe9de92-f6ac-354a-9da4-c5cd98e4a69a",
                        "source_sense_id": "5966bb90-e1bd-3884-8d94-457c31b348ef",
                        "target_lang_word": "choane",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "choane",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "247e9cab-2d43-3f61-b407-9211eca1e822",
                                        "entry_id": "4fb363eb-55ff-36ee-9307-2d8e8d157673",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chez les tétrapodes, arrière-narine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af7f22ea-2a83-3e86-8e5d-af3c54387a62",
                                        "entry_id": "4fb363eb-55ff-36ee-9307-2d8e8d157673",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chez les vertébrés inférieurs, communication entre la bouche et les narines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1995be3-1f24-3575-a4ec-c64898be7e8d",
                                        "entry_id": "4fb363eb-55ff-36ee-9307-2d8e8d157673",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chez les hominidés, orifice postérieur qui fait communiquer la fosse nasale avec le nasopharynx."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8df033f7-62a8-4b40-9ee4-bcc90a13859d",
                                                "sense_id": "b1995be3-1f24-3575-a4ec-c64898be7e8d",
                                                "text": "(Au féminin)… mettez vous au niveau de la choane, le long de la cloison nasale, …."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50d3ca72-7c11-4a5a-b8dc-07d71c46110f",
                                                "sense_id": "b1995be3-1f24-3575-a4ec-c64898be7e8d",
                                                "text": "(Au masculin) Environ 1 à 2 cm crânialement à l'ouverture piriforme , s'étend le méat nasopharyngien , en direction dorsale , vers le choane."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
